@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `bm-ear-nouns`
IMPORT `bm-ear-general-conditions`
IMPORT `bm-ear-part1-material-damage`
IMPORT `bm-ear-fixtures`

-- Tests for Part I, material damage (src:153-242). Every expected value was worked by hand
-- from the text, the scenario figures in bm-ear-fixtures.l4, and the order of arithmetic
-- stated at the head of bm-ear-part1-material-damage.l4 (fork F15), before the assertion
-- was run; the working is written beside each. A failing assertion is a finding.
--
-- Standard figures: item 1 sum insured 10,000,000,000 = full value; Part I deductible
-- 50,000,000; debris sum 200,000,000; total sum insured under Part I 13,500,000,000.
-- The standard loss: restoring 1,000,000,000, value before 8,000,000,000, salvage
-- 50,000,000, incurred 1,000,000,000.

§ `Tests: Part I`

§§ `Cover: the standard loss is covered`

#ASSERT null (`Part I: the grounds on which Bao Minh is not liable for` `the standard loss` `in` `the standard claim`)
#ASSERT `Article 2: payment may now be made for` `the standard loss`

§§ `The insuring clause (src:155-163)`

GIVEN n IS A `The nature of a loss under Part I`
GIVETH A `A loss under Part I`
`the standard loss, of nature` n MEANS
    `a loss of` (`machinery in item` 1) `, which is` n `, costing` `the standard repair costs`

GIVEN l IS A `A loss under Part I`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A ground on which Bao Minh is not liable`
`the Part I grounds for` l MEANS
    `Part I: the grounds on which Bao Minh is not liable for` l `in` (`the standard claim, with losses` (LIST l))

-- Not sudden and unforeseen; not physical; not needing repair.
#ASSERT `the Part I grounds for` (`the standard loss, of nature` (`a loss of nature` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)) EQUALS LIST `Part I: not sudden and unforeseen physical loss or damage`
#ASSERT `the Part I grounds for` (`the standard loss, of nature` (`a loss of nature` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE)) EQUALS LIST `Part I: not sudden and unforeseen physical loss or damage`
#ASSERT `the Part I grounds for` (`the standard loss, of nature` (`a loss of nature` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE)) EQUALS LIST `Part I: repair or replacement is not necessary`
-- An item the schedule does not name (item 9).
#ASSERT `the Part I grounds for` (`a repairable loss to item` 9 `costing` `the standard repair costs`) EQUALS LIST `Part I: the item is not named in the schedule`

§§ `The period: an occurrence after the schedule date (src:56)`

#ASSERT `Part I: the grounds on which Bao Minh is not liable for` `the standard loss` `in` (`the standard claim, for the occurrence` (`an occurrence on` (YMD 2027 1 15) `caused by` (LIST `a cause the policy does not name`))) EQUALS LIST `period of insurance: the occurrence is outside it`

§§ `Part I exclusions 3-6: one trigger and one near miss each (src:181-189)`

GIVEN causes IS A LIST OF `A cause of loss`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A ground on which Bao Minh is not liable`
`the Part I grounds for the standard loss caused by` causes MEANS
    `Part I: the grounds on which Bao Minh is not liable for` `the standard loss` `in`
        (`the standard claim, for the occurrence` (`an occurrence on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `caused by` causes))

-- 3: faulty design excludes; a fault in erection does not; both together exclude (fork F22).
#ASSERT `the Part I grounds for the standard loss caused by` (LIST `faulty design`) EQUALS LIST `Part I exclusion 3: faulty design, defective material or casting, or bad workmanship`
#ASSERT null (`the Part I grounds for the standard loss caused by` (LIST `a fault in erection`))
#ASSERT `the Part I grounds for the standard loss caused by` (LIST `a fault in erection`, `faulty design`) EQUALS LIST `Part I exclusion 3: faulty design, defective material or casting, or bad workmanship`
#ASSERT `the Part I grounds for the standard loss caused by` (LIST `bad workmanship other than a fault in erection`) EQUALS LIST `Part I exclusion 3: faulty design, defective material or casting, or bad workmanship`
-- 4: corrosion excludes; theft does not.
#ASSERT `the Part I grounds for the standard loss caused by` (LIST `corrosion`) EQUALS LIST `Part I exclusion 4: corrosion, wear, oxidation or scaling`
#ASSERT null (`the Part I grounds for the standard loss caused by` (LIST `theft`))
-- 5: cheques excluded; machinery not.
#ASSERT `the Part I grounds for` (`a loss of` (`part of the item numbered` 1 `cheques`) `, which is` `an ordinary repairable loss` `, costing` `the standard repair costs`) EQUALS LIST `Part I exclusion 5: files, drawings, money, securities, packaging and the like`
#ASSERT `the Part I grounds for` (`a loss of` (`part of the item numbered` 1 `packaging materials such as cases, crates and boxes`) `, which is` `an ordinary repairable loss` `, costing` `the standard repair costs`) EQUALS LIST `Part I exclusion 5: files, drawings, money, securities, packaging and the like`
-- 6: discovered only at an inventory.
#ASSERT `the Part I grounds for` (`the standard loss, of nature` (`a loss of nature` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)) EQUALS LIST `Part I exclusion 6: discovered only when an inventory was taken`

§§ `General Condition 5: an item not repaired promptly and properly (src:119-120; fork F12)`

`a loss to an item left unrepaired before` MEANS
    `A loss under Part I` WITH
        `the property`                                                          IS `machinery in item` 1
        `the nature`                                                            IS `an ordinary repairable loss`
        `the costs`                                                             IS `the standard repair costs`
        `the item had earlier been damaged and not repaired promptly and properly` IS TRUE
        `invoices showing the repair or replacement have been produced`         IS TRUE
#ASSERT `the Part I grounds for` `a loss to an item left unrepaired before` EQUALS LIST `GC5: liability for the item had ceased, because an earlier loss was not repaired promptly and properly`

§§ `Article 4: surrounding property (src:237-242)`

#ASSERT null (`the Part I grounds for` `the standard surrounding-property loss`)
-- Not the principal's or a contractor's.
#ASSERT `the Part I grounds for` (`a loss of` (`surrounding property` TRUE FALSE `property of another kind`) `, which is` `an ordinary repairable loss` `, costing` `the standard repair costs`) EQUALS LIST `Article 4: surrounding property not on or near the site, or not the principal's or a contractor's`
-- Construction plant.
#ASSERT `the Part I grounds for` (`a loss of` (`the principal's surrounding property, of kind` `construction or erection plant, machinery or equipment`) `, which is` `an ordinary repairable loss` `, costing` `the standard repair costs`) EQUALS LIST `Article 4: construction or erection plant, machinery or equipment`
-- Connected with construction, not with erection or testing.
#ASSERT `Part I: the grounds on which Bao Minh is not liable for` `the standard surrounding-property loss` `in` (`the standard claim, for the occurrence` (`an occurrence on 1 June 2026, on or near the site` TRUE `, connected with erection or testing` FALSE `, connected with construction` TRUE)) EQUALS LIST `Article 4: not directly connected with the erection or testing of the insured items`
-- No item 4 in the schedule.
#ASSERT `Part I: the grounds on which Bao Minh is not liable for` `the standard surrounding-property loss` `in` (`a claim under` (`the standard policy with schedule` `a schedule without item 4`) `with losses` (LIST `the standard surrounding-property loss`)) EQUALS LIST `Article 4: the value of the surrounding property is not stated at Part I item 4 of the schedule`

§§ `The amount: the standard loss (src:205-216)`

-- Article 2(a): 1,000,000,000 - 50,000,000 salvage = 950,000,000; incurred 1,000,000,000,
-- so not reduced; no average; within item 1's 10,000,000,000; less the deductible
-- 50,000,000 = 900,000,000.
#ASSERT `Article 2: the basis of settlement for` `the standard loss` `under` `the standard policy` EQUALS 950000000
#ASSERT `Part I: the amount Bao Minh is liable to pay for` (`the standard claim, with losses` (LIST `the standard loss`)) EQUALS 900000000

§§ `Article 1: average (src:193-203; fork F23)`

-- Item 1 insured for 8,000,000,000 of 10,000,000,000: 950,000,000 x 0.8 = 760,000,000;
-- less 50,000,000 = 710,000,000.
#ASSERT `Article 1: the proportion of the loss recoverable on` `item 1, underinsured` EQUALS 0.8
#ASSERT `Part I: the amount Bao Minh is liable to pay for` (`a claim under` (`the standard policy with schedule` `a schedule with underinsured item 1`) `with losses` (LIST `the standard loss`)) EQUALS 710000000
-- Item 3: the document does not say what ought to have been insured.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Part I: the amount Bao Minh is liable to pay for` (`the standard claim, with losses` (LIST (`a repairable loss to item` 3 `costing` `the standard repair costs`)))
        BECAUSE "Article 1 states the amount that ought to have been insured only for items 1 and 2, and Article 4 for item 4"
-- Item 4, surrounding property: 200,000,000 less 50,000,000 = 150,000,000; underinsured at
-- 1,000,000,000 of 2,000,000,000: 100,000,000 less 50,000,000 = 50,000,000.
#ASSERT `Part I: the amount Bao Minh is liable to pay for` (`the standard claim, with losses` (LIST `the standard surrounding-property loss`)) EQUALS 150000000
#ASSERT `Part I: the amount Bao Minh is liable to pay for` (`a claim under` (`the standard policy with schedule` `a schedule with underinsured item 4`) `with losses` (LIST `the standard surrounding-property loss`)) EQUALS 50000000

§§ `Article 2: total loss and constructive total loss (src:211-222)`

-- Repair 9,000,000,000 >= value 8,000,000,000: basis (b), 8,000,000,000 - 500,000,000
-- salvage = 7,500,000,000; incurred 9,000,000,000; less 50,000,000 = 7,450,000,000.
#ASSERT `Part I: the amount Bao Minh is liable to pay for` (`the standard claim, with losses` (LIST (`a repairable loss to item` 1 `costing` (`costs: restoring` 9000000000 `, value before` 8000000000 `, salvage` 500000000 `, incurred` 9000000000)))) EQUALS 7450000000
-- A total loss, replaced at a cost of 9,000,000,000: the same 7,450,000,000.
#ASSERT `Part I: the amount Bao Minh is liable to pay for` (`the standard claim, with losses` (LIST (`a loss of` (`machinery in item` 1) `, which is` `a total loss` `, costing` (`costs: restoring` 0 `, value before` 8000000000 `, salvage` 500000000 `, incurred` 9000000000)))) EQUALS 7450000000

§§ `Article 2: temporary repairs, alterations; Article 3: extra charges; the sum insured limb (src:214-235)`

GIVEN c IS A `The costs of a loss under Part I`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Part I amount for the standard repair with costs` c MEANS
    `Part I: the amount Bao Minh is liable to pay for` (`the standard claim, with losses` (LIST (`a repairable loss to item` 1 `costing` c)))

-- Temporary repairs of 100,000,000 forming part of the permanent repairs, not increasing
-- cost: 1,000 + 100 - 50 = 1,050 million; incurred 1,100; less 50 = 1,000,000,000.
#ASSERT `the Part I amount for the standard repair with costs` (`the standard repair, with a part not insured of` 0 `, incurred` 1100000000 `, temporary repairs` 100000000 `forming part` TRUE `increasing cost` FALSE `, alterations` 0 `, extra charges` 0 `, consequential losses` 0) EQUALS 1000000000
-- The same temporary repairs, increasing the cost: nothing for them; 900,000,000.
#ASSERT `the Part I amount for the standard repair with costs` (`the standard repair, with a part not insured of` 0 `, incurred` 1100000000 `, temporary repairs` 100000000 `forming part` TRUE `increasing cost` TRUE `, alterations` 0 `, extra charges` 0 `, consequential losses` 0) EQUALS 900000000
-- Alterations of 200,000,000 within 1,200,000,000 spent: incurred less alterations is
-- 1,000 million, basis 950 million stands; 900,000,000.
#ASSERT `the Part I amount for the standard repair with costs` (`the standard repair, with a part not insured of` 0 `, incurred` 1200000000 `, temporary repairs` 0 `forming part` FALSE `increasing cost` FALSE `, alterations` 200000000 `, extra charges` 0 `, consequential losses` 0) EQUALS 900000000
-- Only 900,000,000 spent, of which 200,000,000 on alterations: limited to 700 million;
-- less 50 = 650,000,000.
#ASSERT `the Part I amount for the standard repair with costs` (`the standard repair, with a part not insured of` 0 `, incurred` 900000000 `, temporary repairs` 0 `forming part` FALSE `increasing cost` FALSE `, alterations` 200000000 `, extra charges` 0 `, consequential losses` 0) EQUALS 650000000
-- 100,000,000 of the repair cost of a kind not included in the sum insured: 850 million;
-- less 50 = 800,000,000.
#ASSERT `the Part I amount for the standard repair with costs` (`the standard repair, with a part not insured of` 100000000 `, incurred` 1000000000 `, temporary repairs` 0 `forming part` FALSE `increasing cost` FALSE `, alterations` 0 `, extra charges` 0 `, consequential losses` 0) EQUALS 800000000
-- Extra charges of 80,000,000, NOT agreed in advance: nothing for them; 900,000,000.
#ASSERT `the Part I amount for the standard repair with costs` (`the standard repair, with a part not insured of` 0 `, incurred` 1080000000 `, temporary repairs` 0 `forming part` FALSE `increasing cost` FALSE `, alterations` 0 `, extra charges` 80000000 `, consequential losses` 0) EQUALS 900000000
-- The same, agreed in writing in advance: 1,030 million; less 50 = 980,000,000.
#ASSERT `Part I: the amount Bao Minh is liable to pay for` (`a claim under` `the standard policy, extra charges agreed` `with losses` (LIST (`a repairable loss to item` 1 `costing` (`the standard repair, with a part not insured of` 0 `, incurred` 1080000000 `, temporary repairs` 0 `forming part` FALSE `increasing cost` FALSE `, alterations` 0 `, extra charges` 80000000 `, consequential losses` 0)))) EQUALS 980000000

§§ `Part I exclusion 2: consequential losses (src:178-179)`

-- 300,000,000 of consequential loss claimed alongside the standard repair: excluded; the
-- amount stays 900,000,000.
`the standard repair with 300,000,000 of consequential loss` MEANS
    `the standard claim, with losses` (LIST (`a repairable loss to item` 1 `costing` (`the standard repair, with a part not insured of` 0 `, incurred` 1000000000 `, temporary repairs` 0 `forming part` FALSE `increasing cost` FALSE `, alterations` 0 `, extra charges` 0 `, consequential losses` 300000000)))
#ASSERT `Part I: the amount Bao Minh is liable to pay for` `the standard repair with 300,000,000 of consequential loss` EQUALS 900000000
#ASSERT `Part I exclusion 2: the consequential losses excluded from` `the standard repair with 300,000,000 of consequential loss` EQUALS 300000000

§§ `Clearance of debris (src:168-170; fork F21)`

-- 300,000,000 of debris clearance, separate sum 200,000,000: 950 + 200 - 50 = 1,100,000,000.
#ASSERT `Part I: the amount Bao Minh is liable to pay for` (`a Part I claim under` `the standard policy` `with losses` (LIST `the standard loss`) `, debris` 300000000 `, paid before` 0 `, other insurance` FALSE `, share` NOTHING) EQUALS 1100000000
-- No separate sum stated: no debris cover; 900,000,000.
#ASSERT `Part I: the amount Bao Minh is liable to pay for` (`a Part I claim under` (`the standard policy with schedule` `a schedule with no sum for debris`) `with losses` (LIST `the standard loss`) `, debris` 300000000 `, paid before` 0 `, other insurance` FALSE `, share` NOTHING) EQUALS 900000000
-- The only loss is excluded (found at an inventory): no debris either; 0.
#ASSERT `Part I: the amount Bao Minh is liable to pay for` (`a Part I claim under` `the standard policy` `with losses` (LIST (`the standard loss, of nature` (`a loss of nature` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE))) `, debris` 300000000 `, paid before` 0 `, other insurance` FALSE `, share` NOTHING) EQUALS 0

§§ `Limits: per item, per occurrence, in aggregate (src:160-163)`

-- Item 2 (sum insured 2,000,000,000): 3,000,000,000 to restore an item worth 4,000,000,000;
-- capped at 2,000,000,000; less 50,000,000 = 1,950,000,000.
#ASSERT `Part I: the amount Bao Minh is liable to pay for` (`the standard claim, with losses` (LIST (`a repairable loss to item` 2 `costing` (`costs: restoring` 3000000000 `, value before` 4000000000 `, salvage` 0 `, incurred` 3000000000)))) EQUALS 1950000000
-- Two losses to item 2 in one occurrence, 1,500,000,000 each: 3,000,000,000 together,
-- capped at 2,000,000,000 for the item; less 50,000,000 = 1,950,000,000.
#ASSERT `Part I: the amount Bao Minh is liable to pay for` (`the standard claim, with losses` (LIST (`a repairable loss to item` 2 `costing` (`costs: restoring` 1500000000 `, value before` 4000000000 `, salvage` 0 `, incurred` 1500000000)), (`a repairable loss to item` 2 `costing` (`costs: restoring` 1500000000 `, value before` 4000000000 `, salvage` 0 `, incurred` 1500000000)))) EQUALS 1950000000
-- A Part I limit for any one occurrence of 500,000,000: 900,000,000 becomes 500,000,000.
#ASSERT `Part I: the amount Bao Minh is liable to pay for` (`a claim under` (`the standard policy with schedule` `a schedule with a Part I occurrence limit of 500,000,000`) `with losses` (LIST `the standard loss`)) EQUALS 500000000
-- 13,200,000,000 already paid of 13,500,000,000: only 300,000,000 remains.
#ASSERT `Part I: the amount Bao Minh is liable to pay for` (`a Part I claim under` `the standard policy` `with losses` (LIST `the standard loss`) `, debris` 0 `, paid before` 13200000000 `, other insurance` FALSE `, share` NOTHING) EQUALS 300000000
-- Two items in one occurrence: item 1 standard (950 million) and item 2 (1,000 million to
-- restore, value 4,000 million, nothing salvaged): 1,950 million, one deductible: 1,900,000,000.
#ASSERT `Part I: the amount Bao Minh is liable to pay for` (`the standard claim, with losses` (LIST `the standard loss`, (`a repairable loss to item` 2 `costing` (`costs: restoring` 1000000000 `, value before` 4000000000 `, salvage` 0 `, incurred` 1000000000)))) EQUALS 1900000000

§§ `Several layers at once`

-- Item 1 underinsured (80%); temporary repairs of 100,000,000 that count; a limit for any
-- one occurrence of 700,000,000. Basis 1,050 million x 0.8 = 840 million; less 50 = 790
-- million; capped at 700,000,000.
`the several-layer loss` MEANS
    `a repairable loss to item` 1 `costing` (`the standard repair, with a part not insured of` 0 `, incurred` 1100000000 `, temporary repairs` 100000000 `forming part` TRUE `increasing cost` FALSE `, alterations` 0 `, extra charges` 0 `, consequential losses` 0)
`the several-layer policy` MEANS `the standard policy with schedule` `a schedule with underinsured item 1 and an occurrence limit of 700,000,000`
#ASSERT `Part I: the amount Bao Minh is liable to pay for` (`a claim under` `the several-layer policy` `with losses` (LIST `the several-layer loss`)) EQUALS 700000000
-- And with other insurance, Bao Minh's proportion determined at one half: 350,000,000.
#ASSERT `Part I: the amount Bao Minh is liable to pay for` (`a Part I claim under` `the several-layer policy` `with losses` (LIST `the several-layer loss`) `, debris` 0 `, paid before` 0 `, other insurance` TRUE `, share` (JUST 0.5)) EQUALS 350000000
-- A covered loss and an excluded loss together: only the covered one counts.
#ASSERT `Part I: the amount Bao Minh is liable to pay for` (`the standard claim, with losses` (LIST `the standard loss`, (`a loss of` (`part of the item numbered` 1 `cheques`) `, which is` `an ordinary repairable loss` `, costing` `the standard repair costs`))) EQUALS 900000000
